# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > l+ l- at LO with QCD=0.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The stated-order half of the Drell-Yan pair. Forbidding the strong
#     coupling outright must select exactly what the default order choice
#     selects for this final state; the two scripts differing only in that
#     constraint is what makes an order-semantics change visible as a diagram
#     count moving on one row and not the other.
#   - Its representative subprocess is u u~ > mu+ mu-, so this is the run whose
#     compiled matrix element every partonic Drell-Yan amplitude check reads:
#     the banked per-helicity table belongs to this row even though the script
#     names a group.
#
# Not used for cross sections or event samples: those are the default-order
# script's dy13 cards, which carry the run cards the hadronic gate shares with
# vibegraph.
generate p p > l+ l- QCD=0
output pp_to_ll_qcd0 -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  done
